{#
  Persistent application-header strip, shown below the back link on every
  page of the accreditation application journey (RA-309 AC03). The
  Material/Site rows match the existing "application-metadata"
  govuk-summary-list--no-border pattern already used on
  task-list/query-task-list. The operator name is unlabelled and set one
  size larger than the page's own h1, per design feedback. A section-break
  rule follows the Site row to set the header apart from the page content
  below it.

  Wrapped in the same grid-row/two-thirds column as the page content below
  it, so the summary-list key/value columns line up with the page's own
  content width rather than stretching the key column to 30% of the full
  page width.

  Params:
    operatorName  (string)
    materialType  (string)
    siteName      (string)
    year          (number)
    materialLabel (string) - defaults to "Material:"
    siteLabel     (string) - defaults to "Site:"
    yearLabel     (string) - defaults to "Year:"
#}
<div class="app-application-header" data-testid="application-header">
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <span class="govuk-caption-m" data-testid="application-header-operator-name">
      {{ params.operatorName }} ( {{ params.materialType }} {{ params.year }} {{ params.siteName }}  )
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
